@page "/components/bubble"

<PageTitle>Bubble — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Bubble</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    One turn in a conversation. An <code>&lt;article&gt;</code> rather than a div: a thread is a list of separately authored things, and that is what lets a screen reader move between them instead of reading the whole thing as one wall.
</p>

<p class="doc-note">
    Message, Bubble, Attachment, Marker and the scroller. The scroller follows the newest message
    only while you are already at the bottom — scroll up to read something and it stops, which is
    the behaviour every chat needs and most get wrong in one direction or the other.
    <code>overflow-anchor</code> does that half in CSS; the browser has had it since 2018.
</p>
